User Follow-up:
can you see from the original reactjs application the api endpoints to get the list of projects, timesheet entries etc

API Discovery Results:
Comprehensive analysis of the Kartoza timesheet project repository revealed the complete API structure:

**Core API Endpoints:**
- Projects: `/project-list/` (GET), `/api/pull-projects/` (POST)
- Timesheet CRUD: `/api/timesheet/` (POST/PATCH), `/api/timelog/` (GET), `/api/delete-time-log/` (POST)
- Activities: `/activity-list/` (GET), `/task-list/{projectId}/` (GET)
- Users: `/user-autocomplete/` (GET), `/api/user-activities/` (GET)
- Submission: `/api/submit-timesheet/` (POST), `/api/clear-submitted-timesheets/` (POST)

**Authentication:**
- Django Allauth: `/accounts/` (login, logout, registration)
- REST Framework: `/api-auth/` (session-based auth)
- CSRF protection required for POST/PUT/DELETE requests

**Additional Features:**
- ERP integration endpoints for ERPNext synchronization
- Reporting: burndown charts, employee summaries
- Schedule management endpoints
- Real-time user activity polling (10-second intervals)

This API structure provides the foundation for potential future integration between our Go TUI application and the existing Django backend, enabling data synchronization and multi-user functionality.

Build System Status:
✅ Makefile created with comprehensive targets
✅ Static build target functional: `make static`
✅ Version information from git integrated
✅ Quality assurance targets (fmt, lint, test, check)
✅ Installation and cleanup targets
✅ Development workflow targets

API Analysis Complete:
✅ Complete endpoint mapping documented
✅ Authentication requirements identified
✅ Data formats and structures understood
✅ Integration possibilities assessed

